        "original_id": "9262189c-4977-5e9f-ad71-8a1c37cacc0e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Munich, Germany; Netherlands\n- Companies: Löwenbräu; Anheuser-Busch InBev\n- Events: Venlo Incident; Georg Elser's failed assassination attempt; Germany's invasion of the Netherlands\n- Organizations: German Nazi government\n- People: Georg Elser; Adolf Hitler\n- Topics: Bürgerbräukeller\n\nFacts:\n- The Bürgerbräukeller was a large beer hall in Munich, Germany.\n- Löwenbräu is a brewery in Munich that is owned by Anheuser-Busch InBev.\n- On 8 November 1939, Georg Elser carried out a failed assassination attempt against German Chancellor Adolf Hitler at the Bürgerbräukeller in Munich, Germany.\n- The German Nazi government later used the Venlo Incident to link Britain to Georg Elser's failed assassination attempt.\n- On 10 May 1940, Germany invaded the neutral Netherlands, and the German Nazi government used the Venlo Incident to help justify that invasion.",
